      <purpose>To record summary information about a single impairment affecting a body function or body structure.</purpose>
      <use>Use to record summary information about a single impairment affecting a body function or body structure.&#xD;
&#xD;
A body function impairment is a problem affecting how a body system or function works. Examples include impairment of vision, hearing, sensation, speech, language, memory, cognition, movement, coordination, balance, emotional function, or psychological function.&#xD;
&#xD;
A body structure impairment is a problem affecting the anatomy of the body, including structural loss, absence, damage, deformity, or other structural abnormality affecting an anatomical part of the body. Examples include limb loss, absence of a body part, tissue loss, structural damage, or deformity of an anatomical structure.&#xD;
&#xD;
The relationship between impairments and diagnoses is not necessarily one-to-one. A single impairment may have multiple underlying causes, and a single diagnosis may give rise to multiple impairments.&#xD;
&#xD;
This archetype is one of a set of three related archetypes designed to represent different aspects of how an individual functions in everyday life. Together, these archetypes support structured representation of functional ability, impairments contributing to functional limitations, and the supports required to enable or assist an individual to perform an activity. The other archetypes are: &#xD;
- OBSERVATION.functional_ability and &#xD;
- EVALUATION.functional_support_requirements.</use>
      <misuse>Not to be used to record the underlying diagnosis, disease, injury, congenital condition, or other health condition associated with the impairment. Use the EVALUATION.problem_diagnosis archetype for this purpose.&#xD;
&#xD;
Not to be used to record an individual's ability to perform an activity or participate in a life situation. Use the OBSERVATION.functional_ability archetype for this purpose.&#xD;
&#xD;
Not to be used to record an assessment of the range of supports required to optimise an individual's ability to perform an activity or participate in a life situation as a result of an impairment. Use the EVALUATION.functional_support_requirements archetype for this purpose.&#xD;
  &#xD;
Not to be used to record information about a symptom or physical sign. Use the CLUSTER.symptom_sign archetype for this purpose.</misuse>
